// Cost-center cross-comparison for Budget Holders/Admin — same
// statistical shape as file 13, one level up: instead of comparing a
// user's average against their team's peer distribution, compares a cost
// center's WINDOWED (trailing 30-day) average daily spend against the
// distribution of that same statistic across every other cost center.
//
// Needs one calculated table (Modeling -> New table) — a per-day,
// per-cost-center rolling window can't be expressed cleanly as a pure
// measure the way file 13's comparison could, since it needs to filter
// rows by date range before grouping, not just re-filter an existing
// aggregation.

// ============================================================
// CALCULATED TABLE
// ============================================================

CostCenterDailyCost =
SUMMARIZE(
    FILTER(
        'llm-usage-container',
        'llm-usage-container'[Date Only] > MAX('llm-usage-container'[Date Only]) - 30
    ),
    'llm-usage-container'[customDimension1],
    'llm-usage-container'[Date Only],
    "DailyCost", CALCULATE([Total Cost (incl. PTU)])
)
// One row per (cost center, day) for the trailing 30 days as of the
// latest data in the model (a snapshot as of last refresh, not a fully
// dynamic per-day rolling window — see the note on Page 9 in
// 04-report-build-guide.md for what a fuller version would need).
// Requires `Date Only` from 10-heatmap-moving-average.dax.

// ============================================================
// THIS COST CENTER'S WINDOWED STATS
// ============================================================

Cost Center Avg Daily Cost (Windowed) =
// CORRECTED: AVERAGE(CostCenterDailyCost[DailyCost]) only averages over
// rows that exist — and CostCenterDailyCost (via SUMMARIZE, above) has a
// row only for (cost center, day) combinations with actual usage, so a
// cost center active on only 10 of the trailing 30 days got its "typical
// daily spend" computed over those 10 days alone, overstating it by up
// to 3x. Fixed the same way 10-heatmap-moving-average.dax's own
// `7-Day Moving Avg Cost` already correctly handles this: SUM the
// existing rows (a missing day contributes $0, which is what you want)
// and divide by the FIXED window size, not by a count of only the days
// that happened to have traffic.
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(
        SUM(CostCenterDailyCost[DailyCost]),
        ALLEXCEPT(CostCenterDailyCost, CostCenterDailyCost[customDimension1])
    ),
    30
)

Cost Center StdDev Daily Cost (Windowed) =
// Scoped caveat, stated plainly rather than silently left: unlike the
// AVG measure above, STDEV.P needs an actual $0 data point per missing
// day to correctly zero-fill (not just a fixed divisor trick), which
// would need a full calendar-day spine joined against
// CostCenterDailyCost — not built here. This measure is therefore still
// computed only over days with actual usage, and understates volatility
// for a cost center with gaps in its trailing-30-day usage. This does
// NOT feed the peer-comparison z-score pipeline below (which now uses
// the corrected AVG measure only) — it's a standalone "how spiky is
// this team's own spend" number, so the residual bias is scoped to this
// one measure, not the outlier detection.
CALCULATE(
    STDEV.P(CostCenterDailyCost[DailyCost]),
    ALLEXCEPT(CostCenterDailyCost, CostCenterDailyCost[customDimension1])
)

// ============================================================
// ORG-WIDE PEER BASELINE (every other cost center's windowed average)
// ============================================================

Org Avg of Cost Center Daily Cost =
AVERAGEX(
    VALUES(CostCenterDailyCost[customDimension1]),
    [Cost Center Avg Daily Cost (Windowed)]
)

Org StdDev of Cost Center Daily Cost =
STDEVX.P(
    VALUES(CostCenterDailyCost[customDimension1]),
    [Cost Center Avg Daily Cost (Windowed)]
)

// ============================================================
// COMPARISON
// ============================================================

Cost Center Cost Z-Score =
DIVIDE(
    [Cost Center Avg Daily Cost (Windowed)] - [Org Avg of Cost Center Daily Cost],
    [Org StdDev of Cost Center Daily Cost]
)

Has Sufficient Data for Cost Center Comparison =
// Guard against a brand-new or tiny org with too few cost centers for
// "typical range" to mean anything statistically.
CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(CostCenterDailyCost[customDimension1]), ALL(CostCenterDailyCost)) >= 3

Is Cost Center Outside Typical Band =
IF(
    NOT [Has Sufficient Data for Cost Center Comparison], "Insufficient data",
    IF(ABS([Cost Center Cost Z-Score]) > 2, "Outside typical range", "Typical")
)
